<title>FRANCE: French gov source-no talks on Italy EMU entry time.</title>
<headline>French gov source-no talks on Italy EMU entry time.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>There are no discussions between European countries about the timing of Italy's entry to European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU), a French government source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;These questions are not under discussion,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;We would like the maximum number of countries to join Economic and Monetary Union as soon as possible, in full respect of the (Maastricht) treaty,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>&quot;We will see in 1998 which countries respect the criteria,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>He had been asked about a report in the Financial Times saying that European Union officials were looking for a face-saving deal that would allow Italy to enter EMU in 2000 or 2001, but not at the 1999 start.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
